{"availability":"available","full":"wangjohn/levenshtein","name":"levenshtein","description":"A comprehensive batch of lint rules for Go, shared across all your repos.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-15T00:50:44Z","updated":"2026-10-03T04:31:48Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["agent-orchestration","agentic","agentic-ai","ai","ai-agents","ai-coding","ai-tools","cicd","lint"],"demo":null,"color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A curated set of Go lint rules and verification checks, easy to hook up to any Go repo.","Coding agents are writing more and more of our code, and I want as much of that code as possible to be verifiable. Good lint rules and automated checks give agents feedback they can act on while they work, and give us more than the agent's word that a change is ready.","I built Levenshtein while setting up a bunch of new Go repos. I wanted one place to keep a high-quality set of rules I could rely on for all of my repos, without researching analyzers and copying lint configs every time. Each repo pins a Levenshtein revision and runs ./verify, so that all my repos use the same rules and tool versions (and updates are easy to roll out everywhere)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wangjohn/levenshtein/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d1eaf209c2ca4ab799e80c409824e0ee1bec20cf5e7b14c3f17533c6c19cf4d8","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A curated set of Go lint rules and verification checks, easy to hook up to any Go repo.","sour